{"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Gnusto"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Getting Started with Gnusto"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GettingStarted"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AnatomyOfAGame","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline"],"title":"Essentials","anchor":"Essentials"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"getting-started.png"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"By the end of this guide you will have a game with two rooms, one object, one rule, and a test that plays it. It assumes you can write basic Swift; it assumes nothing about interactive fiction.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Prefer to start from something that already runs? ","type":"text"},{"code":"bin\/new-game Zwank ~\/dev\/Zwank","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" writes a complete starter package named for your game — then skim this guide for the ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"why"}]},{"text":" behind each piece.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Add Gnusto to your package","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Add-Gnusto-to-your-package"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"These articles describe the engine on ","type":"text"},{"code":"main","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so pin the newest release: ","type":"text"},{"code":"bin\/new-game","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reads it from the repository’s tags, and if a name an article uses fails to compile in your package, the pin is behind the article. Building against a checkout instead (","type":"text"},{"code":"bin\/new-game --dep-path","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") cannot fall behind.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Add Gnusto as a dependency, list it in your executable target, and give the test target the ","type":"text"},{"code":"GnustoTestSupport","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" product (it links the toolchain’s Testing library, so it belongs in test targets only):","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ swift-tools-version: 6.2","import PackageDescription","","let package = Package(","    name: \"MyGame\",","    platforms: [.macOS(.v15)],","    dependencies: [","        .package(url: \"https:\/\/github.com\/HeirloomLogic\/Gnusto\", from: \"0.6.0\")","    ],","    targets: [","        .executableTarget(","            name: \"MyGame\",","            dependencies: [","                .product(name: \"Gnusto\", package: \"Gnusto\")","            ]","        ),","        .testTarget(","            name: \"MyGameTests\",","            dependencies: [","                \"MyGame\",","                .product(name: \"GnustoTestSupport\", package: \"Gnusto\"),","            ]","        ),","    ]",")"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Gnusto needs a Swift 6.2 toolchain and the Swift 6 language mode. The ","type":"text"},{"code":".macOS(.v15)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" floor above is ","type":"text"},{"code":"Synchronization.Mutex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; Linux is tested in CI and needs no platform line. iOS is supported too, at ","type":"text"},{"code":".iOS(.v18)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for the same reason. Add that line if your game is an app rather than a terminal program, and give it an ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/IOHandler"},{"text":" of its own — see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/CustomFrontEnds"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Declare a game","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Declare-a-game"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A game is a single type conforming to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Game"},{"text":". Start with just a title and an intro:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import Gnusto","","struct MyGame: Game {","    let title = \"My First Game\"","    let intro = \"A cool breeze drifts down the hall.\"","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Game"},{"text":" requires an ","type":"text"},{"code":"init()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", but Swift synthesizes it for free as long as every stored property has a default value — which they always will here, since rooms, items, and state are declared with initializers.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Add a room","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Add-a-room"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Declare a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location"},{"text":" as a stored property. The property name (","type":"text"},{"code":"hall","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") becomes the room’s internal identity; the ","type":"text"},{"code":"name(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" trait is what the player sees.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["struct MyGame: Game {","    let title = \"My First Game\"","    let intro = \"A cool breeze drifts down the hall.\"","","    let hall = Location {","        name(\"Entrance Hall\")","        description(\"A long hall of grey stone. A doorway opens to the north.\")","    }","","    var map: WorldMap {","        player.starts(in: hall)","    }","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"map","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" block is where geography and starting positions live. ","type":"text"},{"code":"player.starts(in:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" places the player; without it, the game has nowhere to begin.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Run it","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Run-it"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Two lines turn a game value into a running session:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let world = try GameWorld(game: MyGame())","await REPL(world: world, io: ConsoleIOHandler()).run()"]},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameWorld"},{"text":" validates the game and builds its initial state up front — a mistake like an exit to an undeclared room is caught here, as a thrown ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/BootstrapError"},{"text":", not at runtime. ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/REPL"},{"text":" runs the prompt\/parse\/perform\/print loop, and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ConsoleIOHandler"},{"text":" reads from and writes to the terminal.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Wrap it in a ","type":"text"},{"code":"do","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"catch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in your ","type":"text"},{"code":"main.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import Gnusto","","do {","    let world = try GameWorld(game: MyGame())","    await REPL(world: world, io: ConsoleIOHandler()).run()","} catch {","    print(\"Couldn't start the game: \\(error)\")","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Run ","type":"text"},{"code":"swift run","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and you can already ","type":"text"},{"code":"look","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" around and try to move.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Add a second room and connect them","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Add-a-second-room-and-connect-them"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Exits are declared on locations in the ","type":"text"},{"code":"map","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" block. Each directional method (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location\/north(_:)"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location\/south(_:)"},{"text":", …) is an ordinary property reference, so a typo or a renamed room is a compile error, not a broken game.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let hall = Location {","    name(\"Entrance Hall\")","    description(\"A long hall of grey stone. A doorway opens to the north.\")","}","","let library = Location {","    name(\"Dusty Library\")","    description(\"Shelves sag under mildewed books. The hall lies south.\")","}","","var map: WorldMap {","    hall.north(library)","    library.south(hall)","","    player.starts(in: hall)","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Exits are one-directional by design — declare both "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hall.north(library)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"library.south(hall)"},{"type":"text","text":" if you want the player to be able to walk back."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Add a thing","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Add-a-thing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare an "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item"},{"type":"text","text":" the same way, then place it in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let lantern = Item {","    name(\"brass lantern\")","    adjectives(\"brass\", \"old\")","    description(\"An old brass lantern, its glass sooty but intact.\")","}","","var map: WorldMap {","    hall.north(library)","    library.south(hall)","","    player.starts(in: hall)","    lantern.starts(in: library)","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Now the player can walk "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"north"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"examine lantern"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"take lantern"},{"type":"text","text":", and see it in their "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inventory"},{"type":"text","text":". The "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/adjectives(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" let them type "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"take brass lantern"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"take old lantern","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; a phrase has to end on a noun, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"take brass"},{"type":"text","text":" on its own is not one of them. The last word of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"name(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (“lantern”) is the noun the parser keys on."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Everything you declare is split into words the same way the parser splits what the player types — lowercased, a trailing possessive dropped, every other punctuation mark a separator. So ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"name(\"Mrs. Vane\")"},{"text":" prints its period and answers to ","type":"text"},{"code":"mrs vane","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"adjectives(\"master's\")"},{"type":"text","text":" is the same declaration as "},{"code":"adjectives(\"master\")","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Write the second: a declaration should read the way the parser stores it."}]},{"anchor":"React-with-a-rule","level":2,"text":"React with a rule","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"So far every verb uses its built-in behavior. To add your own logic, write a rule in the ","type":"text"},{"code":"rules","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" block. Rules are ","type":"text"},{"code":"before","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"after","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" hooks attached to a location, an item, or the whole world.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["var rules: Rules {","    lantern.after(.take) {","        say(\"It's heavier than it looks.\")","    }","","    library.before(.go) {","        guard command.direction != .south else { return }","        try refuse(\"There's no exit that way — only back south to the hall.\")","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The first rule runs ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"after","type":"text"}]},{"text":" the player successfully takes the lantern and adds a line of flavor with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/say(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". The second runs ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" movement in the library and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/refuse(_:)"},{"text":"s any direction but south. Inside a rule body, bare identifiers like ","type":"text"},{"code":"command","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"player","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and your own ","type":"text"},{"code":"lantern","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" refer to the live turn — reading and writing them touches the current game state.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To learn what rules can do — the phases, the ordering, and the difference between "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refuse"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reply"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"say"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"end"},{"text":" — read ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WritingRules","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Test it","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Test-it"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A play session is just typed input and printed output, so the natural test plays a scripted session and asserts on the transcript:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import GnustoTestSupport","import Testing","","@testable import MyGame","","struct MyGameTests {","    @Test func theLanternIsWhereTheBreezeSaysItIs() async throws {","        let transcript = try await play(MyGame(), [\"north\", \"take lantern\"])","        expectInOrder(transcript, [\"Dusty Library\", \"Taken.\"])","    }","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"play","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" boots the game and feeds it each command; ","type":"text"},{"code":"expectInOrder","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" asserts the beats appear in order and shows the full transcript when one doesn’t. See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TestingYourGame","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for turn slicing and pinning the random stream.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"A fuller example","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"A-fuller-example"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Gnusto ships with ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Cloak of Darkness"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":", Roger Firth’s classic one-room demonstration game, as its ","type":"text"},{"code":"CloakOfDarkness","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" target. It exercises nearly every feature in a page of code — dark rooms, a wearable cloak, scored actions, a losing state, and per-turn rules — and is worth reading start to finish once the basics click.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Next steps","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Next-steps"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"bin\/new-game","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in the repo — writes the complete starter package this guide builds up to","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AnatomyOfAGame","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — how declarations, identity, and live references fit together","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — exactly what happens each turn","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WritingRules","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — the full vocabulary of game logic","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AddingCustomVerbs","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — teach the parser new words with ","type":"text"},{"code":"#verb","type":"codeVoice"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TestingYourGame","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — transcript tests with GnustoTestSupport","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/CustomStateAndTraits","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — carry your own data on entities and in globals","type":"text"}]}]}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/gnusto\/gettingstarted"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Build and run your first text adventure, one piece at a time.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"kind":"article","references":{"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/adjectives(_:)":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Additional words the parser accepts before the item’s noun."}],"title":"adjectives(_:)","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/adjectives(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/adjectives(_:)","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"adjectives","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":"...) -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ItemTrait","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto9ItemTraitV","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/AddingCustomVerbs":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/addingcustomverbs","title":"Adding Custom Verbs","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AddingCustomVerbs","kind":"article","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Teach the parser words the built-in table doesn’t know.","type":"text"}],"role":"article"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/REPL":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/REPL","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"REPL","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The outer loop: prompt → parse → perform → print, until the game ends or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"input runs out. Holds the only "},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in a Gnusto game."}],"type":"topic","title":"REPL","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/repl","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"REPL","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/say(_:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/say(_:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"say","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Prints a message as part of the turn’s output.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"say(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/say(_:)","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/AnatomyOfAGame":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/anatomyofagame","kind":"article","title":"Anatomy of a Game","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AnatomyOfAGame","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"How a single Swift type becomes a world the engine can run.","type":"text"}],"role":"article"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto":{"abstract":[{"text":"An engine for writing interactive fiction in Swift.","type":"text"}],"title":"Gnusto","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto","role":"collection"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/refuse(_:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/refuse(_:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"refuse","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Never","preciseIdentifier":"s:s5NeverO","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Blocks the current action with a complaint. The default action and any","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"remaining ","type":"text"},{"code":"before","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"after","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" rules are skipped; world time still passes.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"refuse(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/refuse(_:)","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"getting-started.png":{"alt":"A lantern lights an open stone doorway and the stairs beyond.","type":"image","variants":[{"traits":["2x","light"],"url":"\/images\/Gnusto\/getting-started@2x.png"}],"identifier":"getting-started.png"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/GameWorld":{"abstract":[{"text":"The game world: owns all state, serializes all mutation, and runs the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"turn pipeline. The single ","type":"text"},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in a game sits between the REPL and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"this actor.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"GameWorld","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"GameWorld","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameWorld","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/gameworld","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"actor","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"GameWorld","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/CustomStateAndTraits":{"abstract":[{"text":"Carry your own data on entities and in globals, alongside the engine’s closed core.","type":"text"}],"title":"Custom State and Traits","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/CustomStateAndTraits","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/customstateandtraits","type":"topic","role":"article"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/ConsoleIOHandler":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ConsoleIOHandler","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ConsoleIOHandler","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Plain terminal IO.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"ConsoleIOHandler","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/consoleiohandler","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ConsoleIOHandler","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/TestingYourGame":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TestingYourGame","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/testingyourgame","type":"topic","title":"Testing Your Game","abstract":[{"type":"t